nnot be checked must be an explicit application decision."],[1566,"If you are still preparing the instance, start in Deployment. The Platform paths assume an accessible console and permission to perform the operations."],[1542,"If you cannot select the DMS, confirm its creation and your read permissions."],[2271,"If you continue with manual registration, the `Device ID` will be exactly `device-001`."],[1755,"If you enable **Honor Key Usage** or **Honor Extended Key Usages**, Lamassu keeps the values requested by the CSR. If you disable them, it replaces them with the ones defined in the profile."],[679,"If you need retention, search, tamper protection or regulatory export, connect a consumer that persists the events into the system approved by your organization."],[389,"If you receive a 401:"],[1159,"If you receive an identity, check the key, subject, use and connection with the consumer."],[2278,"If you use an intermediate CA, the trusted root must be in `ca.pem` and you must supply the intermediates with `-untrusted intermediates.pem`. This variant is covered in the trust model."],[953,"Implement renewal and recovery and trust updates. The EST reference covers endpoints, formats and ServerKeyGen; troubleshooting helps distinguish transport, admission and persistence failures."],[2022,"Import an existing pair"],[1666,"Import an external CA"],[2036,"Import keys created externally."],[1709,"Import the certificate and, when applicable, its PEM key. Register the CAs needed to identify the issuer. Registering a CA does not install it in external trust stores."],[2074,"Importing lets you register in Lamassu a key generated outside the platform. It is the usual flow in BYOK scenarios, migrations or integration with cryptographic material already in production."],[2226,"In **Certification Authorities**, select **Create New CA** and choose to create a CA with a new key pair."],[1690,"In **Certification Authorities**, select **Create New CA** and choose to generate a new key